      "grammarFocus": "genitive with от",
      "sentenceRef": "Плачу от счастья.",
      "explanation": "'От' always requires genitive case and indicates cause or source: 'от счастья' (from happiness), 'от страха' (from fear), 'от боли' (from pain). This cause-meaning pattern is very common with emotions: 'плакать от радости' (cry from joy), 'дрожать от холода' (shiver from cold). Don't confuse with 'из-за' + genitive, which implies a negative cause.",
      "focusArea": "cases"
    },
